    "created_at": "2016-07-21T10:42:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-21T10:42:52Z",
    "body": "What I said elsewhere is that I think this should become an annotation on a task. The user agent ends up queuing certain tasks in response to user action. It should annotate those tasks (similar to how Fetch annotates tasks) and then APIs can look at that annotation.\n\nThen the standards defining user interaction should decide when to annotate the task.\n\n(I realize we're likely stuck with the current setup for a while, since user interaction standards are extremely lacking and have been for a long time, but I figured I'd mention my thoughts on a better model.)\n",
